1
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:23,390
It's already past noon.

2
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:26,680
Who cares?
It's summer vacation anyway.

3
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:32,090
But we have to pack for band camp.

4
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,540
I really don't feel like going.

5
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:40,770
Huh?

6
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,970
Weren't you looking forward to it?

7
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:45,259
Well, it's a group trip, right?

8
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:47,910
If I can't be alone with you, Miwa,
what's the point?

9
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:52,980
I wanted to cuddle and make out
and do naughty things out in nature.

10
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:58,250
Your mind is in the gutter again.

11
00:01:02,260 --> 00:01:05,330
Come on, Miwa, you like
that stuff too, don't you?

12
00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:10,800
Wait, hold on...

13
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:14,770
Just for a second.

14
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:16,270
Please?

15
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:27,250
Saeko, really...

16
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:31,650
I'll pass.

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:33,500
"How Do We Relationship?"

18
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:38,850
We're here.

19
00:02:38,851 --> 00:02:40,771
[Episode 3: I Don't Get Jealous]
Finally made it!

20
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,320
Man, this is so heavy!

21
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,699
I'll go get the keys.

22
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:44,930
Here, let me take that.

23
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,330
- Oh, thanks.
- Sure.

24
00:02:49,970 --> 00:02:51,439
My sunglasses are missing, too.

25
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:53,419
Did you leave them in the car?

26
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:55,079
- Did you see them?
- Nope.

27
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:58,410
Look, we're not here on vacation.

28
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,219
Even if you're the lead singer,
at least help carry some gear.

29
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,419
But they're my sunglasses!

30
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:03,420
How should I know?

31
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:04,500
Right, Saeko?

32
00:03:12,290 --> 00:03:15,220
Saeko, don't you ever get jealous?

33
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:16,890
Huh?

34
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:19,159
Why would Miwa suddenly fall for a guy now?

35
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:22,530
No, but even if you
know she'd never cheat...

36
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:25,529
Wouldn't you still get mad seeing
her get so cozy with someone else?

37
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:26,530
Whoa, that's heavy.

38
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:29,270
What's wrong with heavy?

39
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:31,520
Hi there, I'm the
suffocating control freak.

40
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,260
A clingy monster.

41
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,510
No thanks, count me out.

42
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:38,416
That stuff is exhausting, whether you're
controlling someone or being controlled.

43
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,899
I've gotten into fights
over jealousy before, too.

44
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:45,450
See? Your girlfriend might
dump you one day, too.

45
00:03:46,050 --> 00:03:47,989
We're madly in love, thank you very much.

46
00:03:47,990 --> 00:03:49,220
Really?

47
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,840
With a face like that, you're
definitely too suffocating.

48
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:54,599
Hey, now I'm pissed!

49
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,039
Oh? You wanna go?

50
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,369
- Here they go.
- Wait!

51
00:03:57,370 --> 00:03:58,769
Possessive chokehold!

52
00:03:58,770 --> 00:03:59,560
Nice one!

53
00:03:59,561 --> 00:04:00,839
Count it for me, Mikkun!

54
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,140
Three! Two! One!

55
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:06,280
- You're making Miwa uncomfortable.
- Yeah, she looks troubled. Knock it off.

56
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:19,179
Alright, let's wrap it up for today.

57
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:20,329
Thanks, good job everyone.

58
00:04:20,330 --> 00:04:22,039
Miwa, right after the pre-chorus...

59
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:23,050
Miwa.

60
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:24,860
Hmm?

61
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:26,940
Let's head back to the room for a sec.

62
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,130
What's up?

63
00:04:32,370 --> 00:04:34,080
Huh? I forgot something.

64
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:44,650
Miwa.

65
00:04:44,810 --> 00:04:45,810
Yeah?

66
00:04:57,230 --> 00:04:58,520
Miwa, do you...

67
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:01,360
Do you ever get jealous or anything?

68
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:03,500
Huh?

69
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:05,499
Where is this coming from?

70
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:06,500
Nothing, just...

71
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:11,240
You saw me messing around with
Lucha and the guys earlier, right?

72
00:05:12,610 --> 00:05:14,010
I was wondering if it bothered you.

73
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:22,990
I don't think I'd be like that.

74
00:05:25,390 --> 00:05:27,560
I trust you, Saeko.

75
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:29,690
I don't think I'd get jealous.

76
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:36,200
Same here.

77
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:38,379
Then we're on the same page.

78
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:39,870
Saeko, wait, hold on...

79
00:05:55,520 --> 00:06:01,760
And besides... I want
you to feel free, Saeko.

80
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:05,290
So I don't want to tie you down.

81
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:22,840
Is something wrong?

82
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:27,320
It's nothing.

83
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:30,990
Just surprised at how compatible we are.

84
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:36,560
Let's head back.

85
00:06:39,330 --> 00:06:40,660
Saeko?

86
00:06:45,730 --> 00:06:47,346
This still looks a bit
rare. Sorry about that.

87
00:06:47,370 --> 00:06:49,640
I'll go grab some more.

88
00:06:51,910 --> 00:06:54,280
Shouldn't you go hang out with Miwa?

89
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,040
It's fine.

90
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:59,050
I feel bad monopolizing her time.

91
00:06:59,850 --> 00:07:01,220
Oh?

92
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,750
What are you pouting about?

93
00:07:04,770 --> 00:07:06,390
I'm not pouting!

94
00:07:07,130 --> 00:07:10,130
Besides, Miwa told me she
doesn't get jealous over me.

95
00:07:10,390 --> 00:07:12,060
We both give each other plenty of space.

96
00:07:13,790 --> 00:07:16,610
Saeko, you're so annoying today.

97
00:07:17,170 --> 00:07:19,230
What? What did you say?

98
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:21,440
Ah, wait!

99
00:07:22,430 --> 00:07:25,070
Saeko, if you have a minute,
could you run an errand for us?

100
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:27,880
- She's definitely not free!
- Ah, wait a second.

101
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:30,250
Hey, wait up! Rika! Seriously!

102
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:33,120
Saeko, please? I can't step away right now.

103
00:07:34,028 --> 00:07:35,455
- Fine, if you insist.
- Sorry about that.

104
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:36,820
Thanks, I really appreciate it!

105
00:07:43,610 --> 00:07:46,060
Saeko, I'll come with you.

106
00:07:46,530 --> 00:07:48,370
You don't have to. Go
hang out with everyone.

107
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:49,760
No.

108
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:51,830
I want to go with you.

109
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,440
Alright then.

110
00:07:57,910 --> 00:07:59,070
Guess I'll let you tag along.

111
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:04,810
This is ridiculously heavy! Did they
seriously expect me to carry all this alone?

112
00:08:05,050 --> 00:08:07,149
Aren't you glad the
two of us came together?

113
00:08:07,150 --> 00:08:08,770
Well, yeah, I guess.

114
00:08:09,650 --> 00:08:10,990
But it's so hot!

115
00:08:12,010 --> 00:08:13,419
- Sorry, sorry. Here.
- Want me to carry that for you?

116
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:14,820
What are you two up to?

117
00:08:15,550 --> 00:08:16,589
Need a hand?

118
00:08:16,590 --> 00:08:17,646
Want us to carry that for you?

119
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:19,389
- Let us take it!
- Wanna eat some corn with us?

120
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:20,789
- You okay?
- We're in a hurry.

121
00:08:20,790 --> 00:08:22,686
At least give us your Insta, then!
Just your Insta!

122
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:24,270
Come on, hook us up!

123
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,310
Please, pretty please?

124
00:08:25,810 --> 00:08:27,540
What's the harm? Come on!

125
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:29,026
Please, just your handle!
What's the big deal? What's the big deal?

126
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,150
Come on, please?

127
00:08:30,170 --> 00:08:31,210
- Pretty please?
- Wait up!

128
00:08:32,130 --> 00:08:35,240
- Let's go.
- It's just Insta! What's the problem?

129
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:49,060
What was their problem?

130
00:08:49,190 --> 00:08:50,330
That really ticked me off.

131
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:55,110
I'm sorry.

132
00:08:56,170 --> 00:08:58,800
Saeko, you ended up carrying my stuff too.

133
00:08:58,970 --> 00:09:01,490
That's what you get for being too cute.

134
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:05,540
You total knockout,
femme fatale, heartbreaker.

135
00:09:06,390 --> 00:09:07,910
Are those supposed to be insults?

136
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,580
All that running wiped me out.

137
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:16,590
Whatever, I'm cracking one of these open.

138
00:09:22,250 --> 00:09:23,250
I'm really sorry.

139
00:09:24,970 --> 00:09:30,010
I wish I could handle guys
like that as well as you do.

140
00:09:31,470 --> 00:09:32,730
No kidding.

141
00:09:32,770 --> 00:09:34,500
Why were you being so polite to them?

142
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:36,840
You've gotta protect yourself.

143
00:09:41,030 --> 00:09:43,250
I'm just kidding.

144
00:09:43,410 --> 00:09:46,350
That helpless side of
you is pretty cute, too.

145
00:09:48,430 --> 00:09:51,130
Anyway, you're carrying
the bags on the way back.

146
00:09:51,170 --> 00:09:52,960
I'm completely exhausted.

147
00:09:54,020 --> 00:09:55,820
Um, Saeko...

148
00:09:55,850 --> 00:09:58,660
We're sprinting all the way back!

149
00:10:04,950 --> 00:10:06,030
Saeko!

150
00:10:15,210 --> 00:10:17,989
What's going on so early in the morning?

151
00:10:17,990 --> 00:10:22,220
- Apparently, his girlfriend just dumped him.
- What?!

152
00:10:22,770 --> 00:10:24,890
Didn't he just say yesterday
they were crazy in love?

153
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:27,360
She dumped him over
the phone out of nowhere.

154
00:10:28,750 --> 00:10:30,990
He can't perform like this!

155
00:10:31,150 --> 00:10:32,230
What do we do?

156
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:33,560
Lucha.

157
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:37,730
Keep your head up!
Today's our debut gig as freshmen!

158
00:10:40,950 --> 00:10:42,200
Sorry, Saeko.

159
00:10:42,570 --> 00:10:44,640
- Can you cover lead vocals too?
- Huh?

160
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:46,710
I told you, there's no way!

161
00:10:47,070 --> 00:10:48,710
Hey, Lucha...

162
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:52,670
Kaori...

163
00:10:53,990 --> 00:10:58,350
I was jealous and controlling...

164
00:11:00,690 --> 00:11:05,190
I just wanted your eyes
on me and no one else!

165
00:11:07,860 --> 00:11:08,860
Um...

166
00:11:10,330 --> 00:11:13,970
Can't we just tell them
we can't play this time?

167
00:11:14,170 --> 00:11:15,770
I mean, under the circumstances...

168
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:20,510
It's all my fault...

169
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:24,510
Forget it...

170
00:11:25,830 --> 00:11:27,350
Forget it, I'll do it.

171
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:30,090
I'll handle both vocals and guitar.

172
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:31,690
What?

173
00:11:32,050 --> 00:11:33,060
Saeko...

174
00:11:34,850 --> 00:11:36,020
Are you sure you can do this?

175
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:37,670
I've got this.

176
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,230
I'll make it work.

177
00:11:42,650 --> 00:11:43,650
Um...

178
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:47,440
If there's anything I can do to help...

179
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,310
Then why don't you sing in my place, Miwa?

180
00:11:55,950 --> 00:11:57,980
Just kidding. I'm joking.

181
00:11:59,130 --> 00:12:00,820
I need to focus on my own.

182
00:12:01,910 --> 00:12:03,050
Sorry.

183
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:35,700
Are you okay?

184
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,100
Are you worried about Saeko?

185
00:12:58,610 --> 00:13:00,910
It's not just worry.

186
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:03,320
I just feel like...

187
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:07,480
Like there's nothing I can do for her.

188
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:12,220
She's always the one helping me.

189
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:19,660
True. Saeko's the type
who handles everything on her own.

190
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:23,830
She's not the kind of
person who leans on others.

191
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:26,400
That might be true, but...

192
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:29,800
I...

193
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:34,880
I feel like if things stay this way,
I'll let Saeko down sooner or later.

194
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:38,050
Or maybe I already have.

195
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:40,020
No way. You're overthinking it.

196
00:13:40,550 --> 00:13:42,680
I want to change.

197
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:45,000
I want to become strong, just like Saeko.

198
00:13:46,050 --> 00:13:49,120
Maybe she's just putting
on a brave face, you know?

199
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:50,360
Oh.

200
00:13:50,490 --> 00:13:51,430
Rika.

201
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:55,500
Tsuruta, the sound guy wants
to talk about the live set.

202
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,800
Oh, I'll be right there.

203
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,440
Miwa.

204
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:04,810
Don't beat yourself up.

205
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:20,020
Sorry, Saeko. We always
dump everything on you.

206
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:21,920
It's fine, don't sweat it.

207
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:24,930
Just don't get mad at
me if I mess up out there.

208
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:34,440
The next band originally had
Lucha on lead vocals...

209
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:40,380
but he got dumped and can't sing,
so Saeko's filling in today!

210
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:49,020
Alright, let's do this!

211
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:53,720
- Yeah!
- I'm so nervous!

212
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:07,300
Okay.

213
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:56,550
♪ The sky dyed in vermilion ♪

214
00:15:56,590 --> 00:15:59,960
♪ Whispers of the night ♪

215
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:03,630
♪ Driving us forward today ♪

216
00:16:03,730 --> 00:16:07,859
♪ Ever onward ♪

217
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:14,970
♪ Our song, blurred by dazzling lights ♪

218
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:19,840
♪ As we hum it softly ♪

219
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:24,200
♪ Blending together, easing the weight ♪

220
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:27,740
♪ Once discovered,
we fled into this place ♪

221
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:31,290
♪ Remembering the times we laughed ♪

222
00:16:31,350 --> 00:16:34,859
♪ We're missing ♪

223
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:38,529
♪ Jewels inside the soda ♪

224
00:16:38,530 --> 00:16:41,990
♪ Gold coins left unspent ♪

225
00:16:42,030 --> 00:16:45,830
♪ A blade so easily snapped ♪

226
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:49,040
♪ A feather hairpin ♪

227
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:53,040
♪ A lone droplet drifting ♪

228
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:56,780
♪ Like our slim odds of winning ♪

229
00:16:56,880 --> 00:17:00,349
♪ And a warm blanket ♪

230
00:17:00,350 --> 00:17:03,199
♪ These are all precious, too ♪

231
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:06,660
♪ Blending together, easing the weight ♪

232
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:10,670
♪ Once discovered,
we fled into this place ♪

233
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:14,000
♪ Remembering the times we laughed ♪

234
00:17:14,030 --> 00:17:17,770
♪ We're missing ♪

235
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:21,540
♪ Made mistakes and lost a few things ♪

236
00:17:21,570 --> 00:17:25,140
♪ Wandering lost, I found you again ♪

237
00:17:25,170 --> 00:17:28,680
♪ Remembering the times we laughed ♪

238
00:17:28,710 --> 00:17:31,450
♪ We're missing ♪

239
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:37,450
♪ We're missing ♪

240
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:43,690
♪ Ever since you've been gone... ♪

241
00:17:44,490 --> 00:17:49,699
Isn't that a bit harsh?
Come on, next up! Let's go!

242
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,229
The upperclassmen were
totally amazing earlier!

243
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:53,800
Cheers!

244
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:57,499
Hey, where did Saeko and Miwa go?

245
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:58,710
Huh?

246
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:01,600
Hey, Saeko.

247
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:03,510
What is going on with you?

248
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,680
You've been acting weird this whole time.

249
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:12,960
Why do you keep pushing me away?

250
00:18:14,370 --> 00:18:15,470
I don't know.

251
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:18,860
What do you mean, you don't know?

252
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:24,270
Do you hate me now?

253
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:25,830
What?

254
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:28,160
Why on earth would you think that?

255
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,190
I can't take this anymore.

256
00:18:31,530 --> 00:18:32,910
I can't think straight.

257
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:35,310
Let's do it, Miwa.

258
00:18:35,590 --> 00:18:36,590
Wait, Saeko...

259
00:18:51,190 --> 00:18:54,260
Saeko, what's gotten into you?

260
00:19:00,690 --> 00:19:02,740
It's okay. You can leave a mark.

261
00:19:04,330 --> 00:19:05,970
As long as it's somewhere nobody can see.

262
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:08,340
You knew?

263
00:19:10,950 --> 00:19:11,950
Yeah.

264
00:19:18,070 --> 00:19:19,070
I'm sorry.

265
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:23,690
Saeko.

266
00:19:29,630 --> 00:19:30,670
I'm sorry.

267
00:19:38,610 --> 00:19:40,690
It's my fault, isn't it?

268
00:19:44,030 --> 00:19:47,020
Because I'm so unreliable,
it made you insecure, didn't it?

269
00:19:47,150 --> 00:19:48,580
You didn't do anything wrong.

270
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:52,590
I'm just being childish.

271
00:19:54,220 --> 00:19:58,790
I was feeling frustrated
and ended up taking it out on you.

272
00:20:02,270 --> 00:20:04,000
Is that really all it was?

273
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:13,710
Maybe because we kept getting interrupted
ever since we got here.

274
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:17,050
So I got sexually frustrated, probably.

275
00:20:22,210 --> 00:20:25,390
Then... do you want to...?

276
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:31,560
Wait, no!
That's definitely not why.

277
00:20:31,910 --> 00:20:35,159
I was treating you so horribly just now.

278
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:36,530
And I hurt you.

279
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Honestly...

280
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:42,200
I'm not nearly as hurt as you think, Saeko.

281
00:20:44,170 --> 00:20:51,380
And if you want to do
it too, Saeko, then I...

282
00:20:53,850 --> 00:20:55,880
What do you mean, "if you want to too"?

283
00:21:08,430 --> 00:21:12,500
Don't you think that makes me awful?

284
00:21:14,350 --> 00:21:15,570
Does it?

285
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:16,910
Yes, it does.

286
00:21:18,890 --> 00:21:21,840
But it's also wonderfully sweet.

287
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:27,650
So pretty.

288
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:30,350
Please turn into Kaori!

289
00:21:31,350 --> 00:21:33,860
What took you guys so
long? What were you doing?

290
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:36,660
Can't you just become Kaori?

291
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:39,160
Let's join in too!

292
00:21:41,670 --> 00:21:43,830
Oh, let's light sparklers!

293
00:21:44,370 --> 00:21:46,739
First one whose spark drops loses, okay?

294
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:47,740
Okay.

295
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:16,970
Remember when I said I wasn't hurt?

296
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,200
Yeah.

297
00:22:20,310 --> 00:22:24,240
That was half a lie.

298
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:25,840
Huh?

299
00:22:29,580 --> 00:22:30,910
I actually felt really lonely.

300
00:22:33,490 --> 00:22:36,250
Wondering if you hated me...

301
00:22:37,450 --> 00:22:39,250
I was really insecure.

302
00:22:43,930 --> 00:22:46,600
Ah, Saeko lost!

303
00:22:48,530 --> 00:22:50,530
I'm always insecure, too.

304
00:22:51,250 --> 00:22:55,170
I worry that you'll hate me, too, so
scared I can't even fall asleep at night.

305
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:59,570
Come on, now you're bluffing again.

306
00:23:02,950 --> 00:23:03,980
Must be nice.

307
00:23:04,580 --> 00:23:06,520
You can be so honest
about your feelings, Miwa.

308
00:23:08,590 --> 00:23:09,590
What?

309
00:23:14,690 --> 00:23:17,190
Miwa, look! Dual wielding!

310
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:18,930
Hey, that's dangerous!

311
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:21,000
- Check this out!
- Wait, hold on, that's dangerous!

312
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:39,780
Saeko, let's go play with everyone.

313
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:41,920
Okay.

314
00:23:45,650 --> 00:23:47,809
[Next Episode]
Tonight, I want to take the lead.

315
00:23:47,810 --> 00:23:50,860
I'm genuinely curious,
why won't you take off your clothes?

316
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:53,429
I heard the person you used to
have a crush on might come too.

317
00:23:53,430 --> 00:23:56,400
Sae-chan,
you're really good at playing it cool.

318
00:23:56,730 --> 00:23:59,640
Next time, it's okay to let yourself cry.
